<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izmail</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izmail is a port town in the Odesa region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiliya">Kiliya</a> branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta. It was an Ottoman fortress commanding the lower Danube, famously stormed by Russian troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-suvorov">Alexander Suvorov</a> in December 1790, and it changed hands several times between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, Moldavia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> before becoming part of Soviet Ukraine in 1940.</p></div>
